  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "sc_pkcs15init_generate_key",
    "file": "opensc/src/pkcs15init/pkcs15-lib.c",
    "description": "Root cause is cleanup of a partially/invalidly initialized private-key object in the error path: sc_pkcs15init_generate_key unconditionally calls sc_pkcs15_free_object(object) at err:, which reaches sc_pkcs15_free_prkey_info -> sc_aux_data_free(&key->aux_data). key->aux_data can contain attacker-influenced garbage (not NULL and not a valid allocation), so sc_aux_data_free dereferences (*data)->type and crashes on a wild read. The bug is missing initialization/sanitization of prkey_info fields (especially aux_data) before any failing path that frees the object.",
    "conditions": "Triggered when fuzzed PKCS#15/profile input drives key-generation setup into an error path after creating/attaching a private-key object but before all nested fields are safely initialized. Then err: cleanup frees that object; sc_pkcs15_free_prkey_info attempts to free aux_data using an invalid pointer value, causing ASan SEGV in sc_aux_data_free. Input must cause malformed object/profile state in fuzz_pkcs15init so object->data->aux_data is non-NULL invalid during cleanup."
  },
